title: AOMEI Update Tampering - Suspicious upgrade-now.exe Execution (UNC7017)
id: 63e76dca-c263-4f04-96fe-77133246c13d
status: experimental
description: >-
    Detects execution of upgrade-now.exe, the payload delivery step of
    UNC7017's short-burst tampering of AOMEI Backupper update infrastructure.
    Between May and July 2026 the actor briefly modified down_html.ini and
    Notifycfg.ini on AOMEI origin servers to redirect Backupper clients to a
    malicious upgrade-now.zip carrying the CROSSROAD downloader and the
    SHINYROAD backdoor; the injected dummy-config bloat forced clients to run
    upgrade-now.exe from the local html directory.
references:
    - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/investigating-ephemeral-supply-chain-tampering/
    - https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/attackers-tampered-with-aomei.html
    - https://cyberworldops.eu/en/attackers-used-brief-aomei-backupper-update-windows-to-deploy
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-17
tags:
    - attack.t1195
    - attack.t1105
    - attack.t1036
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\upgrade-now.exe'
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate AOMEI Backupper upgrade binaries named upgrade-now.exe delivered by the vendor's own update channel
level: high
